course: dictionary
lesson: 9415
title: Squeal: a sound and a secret
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word squeal has more than one meaning. Most often it is a long, high, loud sound made by a person, an animal, or by brakes or tyres. The clues around it tell you which sound is meant.
explain: «In the lumpy little valley the Mole trips and falls with a squeal — he's cut his shin.» The clues are trips, falls and cut his shin, so the squeal is a cry of pain. The same word can also show delight or fright, so always read what happens around it.
explain: Squeal also has a slang meaning: to tell secrets to the police or to someone in charge. In a crime story, «Don't squeal on us» means don't tell on us. When a word has more than one meaning, try each one in the sentence and choose the one that fits.
fact: Squeal can be a verb (to squeal) or a noun (a squeal).
fact: «Squeal» means a long, high, loud sound.
fact: «Squeal with delight» means making a high, happy noise.
fact: «Squeal of brakes» means the high screech of tyres when a car stops hard.
fact: «Squeal on someone» is slang for telling on them to the police or to someone in charge.
exercise: «Of course Toad falls into the water with a splash and a squeal.» What is a squeal here? | A quiet hum like a bee | *A long, high, loud sound | A deep, slow growl | A soft pat on the back
exercise: «A frightened pig squeals very loudly to call for help.» Which feeling does the squeal show? | *Fright | Sleepiness | Boredom | Hunger
exercise: «Tyres squeal when a car brakes hard.» When does the squeal happen? | When a car is parked in the garage | When a car is filled with petrol | When a car is being washed | *When a car brakes hard
test: In a crime story a thief hisses, «Don't squeal on us!» What does squeal on us mean? | Make a high sound of delight | *Tell on us to the police | Sing loudly with us | Run away very fast
test: «Children squeal with delight at the fair.» What does squeal with delight show? | Tiredness and a wish to sleep | Hunger and thirst | Anger and a wish to fight | *Happiness and excitement
exam: Which sentence uses squeal in the slang sense of telling on someone? | The brakes made a squeal on the wet road. | *Nadia decided to squeal to the teacher about the broken window. | The children squealed with laughter at the joke. | The pig gave a loud squeal in the mud.
